Description: Ngó Sen for GNOME, a Vietnamese input method for IBus
 Ngó Sen for GNOME types Vietnamese through IBus, the input method GNOME
 comes with. It types straight into apps that report the text around the
 cursor and underlines the word being typed elsewhere; the typing mode can
 be picked for each app. A tap of Ctrl+Shift switches between English and
 Vietnamese.
